{"id":"refine_20260929114522909","summary":"Saved a global memory for the demonstrated ARC pattern-stamping task family.","rationale":"The demos support identifying a compact source pattern and stamping its non-background cells at scattered markers, with the marker aligned to the source pattern’s central anchor color; the solved test confirms this for a 3×3 pattern containing a distinct zero.","expectedOutcome":"Future ARC instances with this structure should be solved by preserving the source pattern and stamping its cells around each marker; validate the inferred background, anchor alignment, and all marker placements against any available demos.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_stamp_a_compact_pattern_at_scattered_markers","title":"ARC: stamp a compact pattern at scattered markers","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background, one compact source pattern, and scattered single-cell markers, consider a pattern-stamping rule: preserve the source and copy its non-background cells around each marker. Infer the background from the grid and identify the source pattern's anchor, often its central cell; align that anchor with each marker. The marker may be replaced by the source anchor's color. Include distinct cells that happen to be 0 when 0 is not the background. Demonstrated variants: a 3×3 pattern stamped at 1 markers, a horizontal 8-3-9 pattern stamped at 7 markers (marker aligns to 3), and a vertical 8/1 pattern stamped at 3 markers. Verify orientation, anchor, and which cells count as background from the input and demos rather than assuming all patterns are centered.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"This reusable rule is directly supported by multiple demo variants and a correctly solved instance.","after":{"id":"arc_stamp_a_compact_pattern_at_scattered_markers","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: stamp a compact pattern at scattered markers","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background, one compact source pattern, and scattered single-cell markers, consider a pattern-stamping rule: preserve the source and copy its non-background cells around each marker. Infer the background from the grid and identify the source pattern's anchor, often its central cell; align that anchor with each marker. The marker may be replaced by the source anchor's color. Include distinct cells that happen to be 0 when 0 is not the background. Demonstrated variants: a 3×3 pattern stamped at 1 markers, a horizontal 8-3-9 pattern stamped at 7 markers (marker aligns to 3), and a vertical 8/1 pattern stamped at 3 markers. Verify orientation, anchor, and which cells count as background from the input and demos rather than assuming all patterns are centered.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:45:34.936Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:45:34.936Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929114755758","summary":"Saved a global memory for the demonstrated row-and-column marker-connecting rule.","rationale":"Multiple demonstrations show that, on a uniform-background grid, gaps between same-color markers are filled along each row and column with color 3, preserving markers and leaving other cells unchanged; the convex-hull guess was incorrect.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances with this structure should be solved by filling only the horizontal and vertical intervals between the outermost markers on each line; validate marker preservation and untouched cells against the demonstrations.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_connect_collinear_markers_rows_columns","title":"ARC: connect collinear markers along rows and columns","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and scattered markers of one color, inspect each row and each column independently. If a line contains at least two markers, fill every background cell between its outermost markers with color 3, preserving marker cells. Leave all cells outside those intervals unchanged. Demonstrations confirm horizontal and vertical fills, including long spans. A convex-hull fill guess failed for this task family; do not use it as a substitute for the row/column interval rule.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"This rule is supported by multiple demonstrations and solved the task after the convex-hull hypothesis was rejected.","after":{"id":"arc_connect_collinear_markers_rows_columns","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: connect collinear markers along rows and columns","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and scattered markers of one color, inspect each row and each column independently. If a line contains at least two markers, fill every background cell between its outermost markers with color 3, preserving marker cells. Leave all cells outside those intervals unchanged. Demonstrations confirm horizontal and vertical fills, including long spans. A convex-hull fill guess failed for this task family; do not use it as a substitute for the row/column interval rule.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:48:00.817Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:48:00.817Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929114919023","summary":"Saved a global ARC memory for aligned-panel overlap tasks separated by a single-color divider.","rationale":"Three demonstrations and a correctly solved task support the rule: identify the color shared by both panels, then mark cells where both aligned panels contain that color.","expectedOutcome":"Future tasks with aligned panels should be solved by verifying the separator and panel dimensions, deriving the shared color from both palettes, and outputting that color with 3 at matching cells; validate against demonstrations when available.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_aligned_panels_shared_color_overlap","title":"ARC: mark shared-color overlaps in aligned panels","content":"For ARC grids divided into two aligned panels by a single-color separator, first confirm the separator orientation and that the panels have matching dimensions. Determine which color occurs in both panel palettes; do not assume it is the most frequent color. Create an output with the shared color as the background, and place color 3 at each corresponding position where both panels contain that shared color. Preserve panel alignment when comparing cells. This rule was validated on three demonstrations and a successful task.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Captures a reusable panel-comparison rule demonstrated repeatedly and confirmed by a correct submission.","after":{"id":"arc_aligned_panels_shared_color_overlap","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: mark shared-color overlaps in aligned panels","content":"For ARC grids divided into two aligned panels by a single-color separator, first confirm the separator orientation and that the panels have matching dimensions. Determine which color occurs in both panel palettes; do not assume it is the most frequent color. Create an output with the shared color as the background, and place color 3 at each corresponding position where both panels contain that shared color. Preserve panel alignment when comparing cells. This rule was validated on three demonstrations and a successful task.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:49:28.520Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:49:28.520Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929114949698","summary":"Added a global ARC memory for demo-verified whole-grid recoloring of backgrounds and markers.","rationale":"A demonstration showed every background cell changing to the marker color and every marker changing to 0; the same mapping correctly solved the test grid, while an earlier connection rule failed.","expectedOutcome":"Future similar tasks should use a demonstration to verify the color mapping, transform every cell while preserving dimensions, and avoid connecting markers unless the examples support it.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_recolor_background_and_markers_using_a_demonstrated_color_map","title":"ARC: recolor background and markers using a demonstrated color map","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and scattered single-cell markers of another color, consider a whole-grid recoloring rule when a demonstration supports it: map every background cell to the marker color and every marker cell to 0. Infer the exact mapping from the input-output pair, then apply it to every cell and preserve grid dimensions. Do not connect markers or otherwise alter their positions unless demonstrations show that behavior. Evidence: an input using colors 5 (background) and 4 (markers) produced 4 (former background) and 0 (former markers); applying the same mapping to a test with colors 5 and 9 solved it. If the rule is ambiguous, request a demonstration rather than assuming a geometric marker rule.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Persists a demonstrated reusable recoloring rule and guards against an unsupported marker-connection interpretation.","after":{"id":"arc_recolor_background_and_markers_using_a_demonstrated_color_map","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: recolor background and markers using a demonstrated color map","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and scattered single-cell markers of another color, consider a whole-grid recoloring rule when a demonstration supports it: map every background cell to the marker color and every marker cell to 0. Infer the exact mapping from the input-output pair, then apply it to every cell and preserve grid dimensions. Do not connect markers or otherwise alter their positions unless demonstrations show that behavior. Evidence: an input using colors 5 (background) and 4 (markers) produced 4 (former background) and 0 (former markers); applying the same mapping to a test with colors 5 and 9 solved it. If the rule is ambiguous, request a demonstration rather than assuming a geometric marker rule.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:49:55.331Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:49:55.331Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929115053817","summary":"Updated the global ARC pattern-stamping memory with the demo-verified centered, same-orientation stamping rule.","rationale":"The test was solved correctly by preserving the 3×3 source pattern and stamping its non-background cells centered on each isolated marker; the source background remained transparent. Boundary clipping and overlap behavior were not exercised by this example, so they should be treated as implementation considerations rather than demo-confirmed details.","expectedOutcome":"Future similar ARC tasks should preserve the source, stamp its non-background cells centered on each marker in the same orientation, and keep the grid dimensions fixed; validate boundary and overlap behavior against any available demonstrations.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_stamp_a_compact_pattern_at_scattered_markers","title":"ARC: stamp a compact pattern at scattered markers","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background, one compact source pattern, and scattered single-cell markers, consider a pattern-stamping rule when demonstrations support it. Preserve the source pattern and replace each isolated marker by stamping the source's non-background cells centered on that marker, in the same orientation. Treat source-background cells as transparent and keep grid dimensions fixed. Clip stamps at grid boundaries if necessary; if stamps overlap, apply the pattern consistently while preserving non-background cells. In a verified task, this rule used a centered 3×3 source pattern and solved correctly. Check demonstrations for anchor alignment and any boundary or overlap cases before relying on those behaviors.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"A test instance was solved correctly using centered, same-orientation stamping with transparent source-background cells; boundary clipping and overlaps are useful considerations but were not demonstrated.","before":{"id":"arc_stamp_a_compact_pattern_at_scattered_markers","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: stamp a compact pattern at scattered markers","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background, one compact source pattern, and scattered single-cell markers, consider a pattern-stamping rule: preserve the source and copy its non-background cells around each marker. Infer the background from the grid and identify the source pattern's anchor, often its central cell; align that anchor with each marker. The marker may be replaced by the source anchor's color. Include distinct cells that happen to be 0 when 0 is not the background. Demonstrated variants: a 3×3 pattern stamped at 1 markers, a horizontal 8-3-9 pattern stamped at 7 markers (marker aligns to 3), and a vertical 8/1 pattern stamped at 3 markers. Verify orientation, anchor, and which cells count as background from the input and demos rather than assuming all patterns are centered.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:45:34.936Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:45:34.936Z","version":1},"after":{"id":"arc_stamp_a_compact_pattern_at_scattered_markers","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: stamp a compact pattern at scattered markers","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background, one compact source pattern, and scattered single-cell markers, consider a pattern-stamping rule when demonstrations support it. Preserve the source pattern and replace each isolated marker by stamping the source's non-background cells centered on that marker, in the same orientation. Treat source-background cells as transparent and keep grid dimensions fixed. Clip stamps at grid boundaries if necessary; if stamps overlap, apply the pattern consistently while preserving non-background cells. In a verified task, this rule used a centered 3×3 source pattern and solved correctly. Check demonstrations for anchor alignment and any boundary or overlap cases before relying on those behaviors.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:45:34.936Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:51:01.714Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929115240206","summary":"Saved a global ARC memory for recoloring the trailing background after truncated horizontal color runs.","rationale":"Two demonstrations and the correctly solved test support recoloring only the background cells to the right of a row’s rightmost contrasting-color cell, while preserving other cells and rows.","expectedOutcome":"Future matching ARC tasks can apply the row-local rule; validate the background and contrasting color, preserve dimensions, and leave full-width rows unchanged.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_recolor_trailing_background_after_horizontal_run","title":"ARC: recolor background after truncated horizontal runs","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and horizontal rows of a contrasting color starting at the left edge, consider recoloring the background cells to the right of a row’s rightmost contrasting-color cell to color 1 when demonstrations support it. Preserve all cells through that rightmost cell—including any internal gaps—along with other rows and grid dimensions. Leave full-width rows unchanged. Verify the color mapping and row-local behavior against examples.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"The rule was supported by two demonstrations and a correct test submission.","after":{"id":"arc_recolor_trailing_background_after_horizontal_run","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: recolor background after truncated horizontal runs","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and horizontal rows of a contrasting color starting at the left edge, consider recoloring the background cells to the right of a row’s rightmost contrasting-color cell to color 1 when demonstrations support it. Preserve all cells through that rightmost cell—including any internal gaps—along with other rows and grid dimensions. Leave full-width rows unchanged. Verify the color mapping and row-local behavior against examples.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:52:47.020Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:52:47.020Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929115327579","summary":"Created a global ARC memory for finding and recoloring exact translated copies of a compact object shape in noisy grids.","rationale":"The solved task demonstrated that the colored polyomino acts as a template: enumerate translations whose entire shape overlays the designated background color, recolor those matched cells, and preserve the source and all other cells.","expectedOutcome":"Future similar puzzles should be solved by checking complete template footprints at every valid translation rather than relying on visual guesses; validate that only full matches are recolored and dimensions and unrelated cells remain unchanged.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_find_and_recolor_exact_template_copies_in_noisy_grids","title":"ARC: find and recolor exact template copies in noisy grids","content":"For ARC grids with noisy background cells and a compact colored object/polyomino, consider using the object's exact cell shape as a template when demonstrations support it. Enumerate every valid translation of the template and accept a match only when every template cell overlays the designated background color. Recolor the matched template cells to the object's color; preserve the source object and all other cells, and keep dimensions unchanged. Validate by checking the complete footprint at each translation, including that partial matches are not recolored.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"This rule solved a demonstrated task where a template shape occurred at translations over uniform-background cells amid unrelated noise.","after":{"id":"arc_find_and_recolor_exact_template_copies_in_noisy_grids","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: find and recolor exact template copies in noisy grids","content":"For ARC grids with noisy background cells and a compact colored object/polyomino, consider using the object's exact cell shape as a template when demonstrations support it. Enumerate every valid translation of the template and accept a match only when every template cell overlays the designated background color. Recolor the matched template cells to the object's color; preserve the source object and all other cells, and keep dimensions unchanged. Validate by checking the complete footprint at each translation, including that partial matches are not recolored.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:53:32.242Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:53:32.242Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929115411866","summary":"Added a global ARC memory for moving a compact object next to a full color-2 stripe and drawing a color-8 trail beyond it.","rationale":"Two demonstrations established the same rule in horizontal and vertical orientations, and the test was solved by applying the rule while preserving the stripe and clearing the object's original position.","expectedOutcome":"Future matching tasks should move the object intact to the stripe-facing side, add the full perpendicular color-8 trail on the far side, and preserve unrelated cells; validate the orientation and placement against demonstrations.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_move_object_adjacent_to_color2_stripe_with_color8_trail","title":"ARC: move an object beside a full color-2 stripe and add a color-8 trail","content":"For ARC grids with a full horizontal or vertical color-2 stripe and a separate compact object or run on a uniform background, consider the demonstrated relocation rule. Move the object, preserving its shape and color, to become immediately adjacent to the stripe on the object's side of it. Paint the next full row or column beyond the relocated object, away from the stripe, color 8. Clear the object's original cells to the background; preserve the stripe and unrelated cells. Infer orientation and side from the input, and use demonstrations to verify the relocation and trail placement.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"The horizontal and vertical demonstrations both support this reusable transformation, and it correctly predicted the solved test output.","after":{"id":"arc_move_object_adjacent_to_color2_stripe_with_color8_trail","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: move an object beside a full color-2 stripe and add a color-8 trail","content":"For ARC grids with a full horizontal or vertical color-2 stripe and a separate compact object or run on a uniform background, consider the demonstrated relocation rule. Move the object, preserving its shape and color, to become immediately adjacent to the stripe on the object's side of it. Paint the next full row or column beyond the relocated object, away from the stripe, color 8. Clear the object's original cells to the background; preserve the stripe and unrelated cells. Infer orientation and side from the input, and use demonstrations to verify the relocation and trail placement.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:54:18.486Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:54:18.486Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929115600367","summary":"Created a global memory for demonstration-verified one-row downward translation of ARC grids.","rationale":"The demo showed the entire grid shifted down by one row, with the top row filled by the background and content past the bottom clipped; applying that rule solved the test correctly.","expectedOutcome":"For future tasks with demonstrations supporting this exact transformation, shift every cell down one row without wrapping, preserve dimensions, and verify the full result against the demo.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_shift_grid_down_one_row","title":"ARC: shift a grid down one row when demonstrations support it","content":"For an ARC grid where a demonstration output is exactly the input shifted down one row, apply that transformation to every cell: fill the top row with the original background color, copy each input row to the row below it, and discard the bottom input row as it moves beyond the grid. Do not wrap cells around. Preserve grid dimensions. Confirm the rule by comparing the entire transformed grid to the demonstration before applying it to a test input.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"A demo-verified one-row downward translation solved the test instance correctly and is a reusable ARC transformation.","after":{"id":"arc_shift_grid_down_one_row","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: shift a grid down one row when demonstrations support it","content":"For an ARC grid where a demonstration output is exactly the input shifted down one row, apply that transformation to every cell: fill the top row with the original background color, copy each input row to the row below it, and discard the bottom input row as it moves beyond the grid. Do not wrap cells around. Preserve grid dimensions. Confirm the rule by comparing the entire transformed grid to the demonstration before applying it to a test input.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:56:04.803Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:56:04.803Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929120618899","summary":"Created a global ARC memory for demo-supported rectangle denoising, with a caution prompted by repeated failure on one instance.","rationale":"Eight demos showed rectangular patches repaired through their bounding boxes and stray alien-color cells changed to the dominant background. The attempted rule did not solve the test instance, so the memory should present it as a hypothesis to verify rather than a complete rule.","expectedOutcome":"Future solvers can recognize this demonstrated pattern while checking component boundaries and seeking additional task-specific structure before submitting.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_denoise_rectangular_patches_and_remove_speckles","title":"ARC: denoise rectangular patches and remove speckles, with verification","content":"For ARC grids where demonstrations show a dominant background, rectangular patches, and scattered alien-color cells, consider reconstructing each supported patch as a solid rectangle and replacing outliers outside patches with the dominant background. Preserve the grid dimensions and any demonstrated background-colored patches. Treat this as a demo-supported hypothesis, not a universal rule: verify component boundaries, patch colors and extents, and whether apparent patches overlap or touch. In one instance, bounding-box reconstruction remained incorrect after repeated submissions, so check for an additional task-specific rule and validate the complete candidate against all available demonstrations before submitting.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"The eight demonstrations support this recurring denoising pattern, while the failed test instance justifies an explicit validation caution.","after":{"id":"arc_denoise_rectangular_patches_and_remove_speckles","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: denoise rectangular patches and remove speckles, with verification","content":"For ARC grids where demonstrations show a dominant background, rectangular patches, and scattered alien-color cells, consider reconstructing each supported patch as a solid rectangle and replacing outliers outside patches with the dominant background. Preserve the grid dimensions and any demonstrated background-colored patches. Treat this as a demo-supported hypothesis, not a universal rule: verify component boundaries, patch colors and extents, and whether apparent patches overlap or touch. In one instance, bounding-box reconstruction remained incorrect after repeated submissions, so check for an additional task-specific rule and validate the complete candidate against all available demonstrations before submitting.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:06:24.662Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:06:24.662Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929120702706","summary":"Added a global ARC memory for demo-supported replication of a populated compartment across equal-sized divider-separated regions.","rationale":"In task-c0efe931, a demonstration showed a region copied across a horizontal divider; the test grid had a 3×3 array of equal compartments, and replicating the populated compartment into every compartment solved the task correctly.","expectedOutcome":"Future similar tasks should identify divider lines and equal-sized compartments, use demonstrations to verify the replication rule, and copy the source region while preserving dividers and grid dimensions.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_replicate_patterns_across_divider_separated_compartments","title":"ARC: replicate patterns across divider-separated compartments","content":"When demonstrations support copying a complete region across a divider, and a task grid is divided by full single-color lines into equal-sized compartments with one populated region, consider copying that region into every matching compartment. Verify compartment dimensions, divider positions, source alignment, and which cells are background before applying the rule. Preserve divider lines, dimensions, and the pattern's alignment within each compartment. Evidence: in task-c0efe931, a demo copied a five-row pattern across a full horizontal line; the test had a 3×3 array of equal 5×9 compartments separated by color-3 lines, and copying the populated bottom-right compartment into all compartments solved the task.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"The demonstrated transformation and correct test solution support a reusable compartment-replication pattern.","after":{"id":"arc_replicate_patterns_across_divider_separated_compartments","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: replicate patterns across divider-separated compartments","content":"When demonstrations support copying a complete region across a divider, and a task grid is divided by full single-color lines into equal-sized compartments with one populated region, consider copying that region into every matching compartment. Verify compartment dimensions, divider positions, source alignment, and which cells are background before applying the rule. Preserve divider lines, dimensions, and the pattern's alignment within each compartment. Evidence: in task-c0efe931, a demo copied a five-row pattern across a full horizontal line; the test had a 3×3 array of equal 5×9 compartments separated by color-3 lines, and copying the populated bottom-right compartment into all compartments solved the task.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:07:07.410Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:07:07.410Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929120931523","summary":"Added a global memory for demo-verified, exact-orientation template stamping into zero-valued matches.","rationale":"The instance was solved by matching the seed’s occupied-cell offsets at translations where every corresponding input cell was zero, then recoloring only those cells. Including rotated or reflected variants led to an incorrect submission.","expectedOutcome":"For future similar ARC tasks, derive the template from the special-color seed, scan valid translations in the same orientation for all-zero matches, preserve the seed and all other cells, and validate against demonstrations.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_stamp_seed_shape_at_zero_template_matches_same_orientation","title":"ARC: stamp a seed shape at exact-orientation zero matches","content":"When demonstrations support this rule, treat the cells of a special-color seed object as a template. Record the occupied-cell offsets relative to the seed's bounding box, then scan every valid translation in the input for locations where all those offsets contain background 0. Recolor only the matched template cells to the seed color. Keep the template in exactly its original orientation: do not rotate or reflect it. Preserve the seed, grid dimensions, and all unrelated cells. Confirm the rule and target color against demonstrations before applying; do not generalize to other backgrounds or transformations without evidence.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"The demonstrated task was solved by exact-orientation, all-zero template matching; the attempt that included rotations and reflections was incorrect.","after":{"id":"arc_stamp_seed_shape_at_zero_template_matches_same_orientation","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: stamp a seed shape at exact-orientation zero matches","content":"When demonstrations support this rule, treat the cells of a special-color seed object as a template. Record the occupied-cell offsets relative to the seed's bounding box, then scan every valid translation in the input for locations where all those offsets contain background 0. Recolor only the matched template cells to the seed color. Keep the template in exactly its original orientation: do not rotate or reflect it. Preserve the seed, grid dimensions, and all unrelated cells. Confirm the rule and target color against demonstrations before applying; do not generalize to other backgrounds or transformations without evidence.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:09:36.530Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:09:36.530Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929121725692","summary":"Added a global ARC memory for demonstration-verified short-gap completion between aligned marker groups.","rationale":"The task was solved by adding color 2 only in supported short horizontal or vertical gaps; repeated submissions that filled longer gaps or assumed a complete bounding-box frame were incorrect. Across the demonstrations, gap behavior varies, so the rule should be inferred rather than generalized from the test alone.","expectedOutcome":"Future solvers can recognize these line-gap completion tasks, infer which gap lengths and alignments are supported by demonstrations, and avoid overfilling long gaps or drawing an unsupported bounding-box frame.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_complete_short_gaps_between_aligned_marker_groups","title":"ARC: complete demonstration-supported short gaps between aligned marker groups","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and scattered markers, demonstrations may show color 2 inserted into short background gaps between aligned groups of markers, horizontally or vertically. Preserve the original markers and change only demonstrated gap cells. Infer the permitted gap length, alignment, and any group-size conditions from the demonstrations; do not automatically connect every collinear pair or draw a complete bounding-box frame. In one instance, gaps of up to two background cells were filled, while longer interior gaps remained unchanged. Treat that threshold as instance-specific, not a universal rule.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"The successful output filled only selected short aligned gaps; several incorrect attempts overfilled longer intervals or relied on an unsupported frame interpretation.","after":{"id":"arc_complete_short_gaps_between_aligned_marker_groups","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: complete demonstration-supported short gaps between aligned marker groups","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and scattered markers, demonstrations may show color 2 inserted into short background gaps between aligned groups of markers, horizontally or vertically. Preserve the original markers and change only demonstrated gap cells. Infer the permitted gap length, alignment, and any group-size conditions from the demonstrations; do not automatically connect every collinear pair or draw a complete bounding-box frame. In one instance, gaps of up to two background cells were filled, while longer interior gaps remained unchanged. Treat that threshold as instance-specific, not a universal rule.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:17:35.801Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:17:35.801Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929121854370","summary":"Clarified the existing global memory for connecting collinear ARC markers, including interval indexing and preserving endpoints.","rationale":"The demonstrations confirmed filling background cells between aligned markers, and the first submission exposed an off-by-one omission. A related global memory already exists, so updating it avoids a redundant duplicate.","expectedOutcome":"Future solvers should fill every strictly interior cell between aligned markers, preserve marker cells and unrelated background, and check interval boundaries against the examples.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_connect_collinear_markers_rows_columns","title":"ARC: connect collinear markers with careful interval boundaries","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and scattered markers of one color, inspect each row and column independently. When a line contains at least two markers, fill every background cell strictly between the outermost markers with color 3; equivalently, fill the intervals between consecutive markers. Preserve the marker cells and all cells outside those intervals. Check indexing carefully: between positions a and b, fill a+1 through b-1, never the endpoints. For example, markers at rows 1 and 4 require filling rows 2 and 3. Apply only when demonstrations support this rule, and preserve dimensions.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Incorporates demo-confirmed interval behavior and guards against the off-by-one error observed in this task.","before":{"id":"arc_connect_collinear_markers_rows_columns","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: connect collinear markers along rows and columns","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and scattered markers of one color, inspect each row and each column independently. If a line contains at least two markers, fill every background cell between its outermost markers with color 3, preserving marker cells. Leave all cells outside those inte