{"id":"refine_20260929121925909","summary":"Added a global ARC memory for demonstrations that support horizontal-only gap filling between aligned markers.","rationale":"The instance’s first submission incorrectly filled vertical alignments, while the corrected output filled only horizontal gaps; the demo establishes that direction must be inferred rather than assumed.","expectedOutcome":"Future solvers can preserve incidental vertical alignments when the demonstrated rule is horizontal-only, and request a demo when the direction remains ambiguous.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_fill_horizontal_marker_gaps_only_when_demonstrated","title":"ARC: fill horizontal marker gaps only when demonstrations support that direction","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and scattered markers of one color, when demonstrations show color 2 filling only horizontal gaps between markers on the same row, fill strictly interior background cells between consecutive markers in each qualifying row. Preserve marker endpoints and all other cells. Do not infer vertical connections merely from shared columns: incidental vertical alignments may remain unchanged. Infer direction from the examples; if row-versus-column behavior is ambiguous, request a demonstration rather than guessing.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"A solved instance showed horizontal-only interpolation, and an initial incorrect attempt added unsupported vertical interpolation.","after":{"id":"arc_fill_horizontal_marker_gaps_only_when_demonstrated","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: fill horizontal marker gaps only when demonstrations support that direction","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and scattered markers of one color, when demonstrations show color 2 filling only horizontal gaps between markers on the same row, fill strictly interior background cells between consecutive markers in each qualifying row. Preserve marker endpoints and all other cells. Do not infer vertical connections merely from shared columns: incidental vertical alignments may remain unchanged. Infer direction from the examples; if row-versus-column behavior is ambiguous, request a demonstration rather than guessing.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:19:30.168Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:19:30.168Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929125644542","summary":"Create a global ARC memory for the demonstrated transformation involving offset parallel border segments and projected marker rays.","rationale":"The task’s demonstrations support recoloring special markers to 4, extending their original color toward an associated border, and drawing corresponding lines at aligned offsets; the solved instance confirms that projected lines can extend to an edge lacking a border segment.","expectedOutcome":"Future solvers can recognize this geometry, infer the segment orientation and coordinate mapping from demonstrations, and verify full line endpoints and preserved cells before submission.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_project_marker_rays_between_offset_border_segments","title":"ARC: project marker rays between offset parallel border segments","content":"For ARC grids where demonstrations show two equal-length, parallel, offset border segments and special-color markers, consider a projection rule. Infer which segment corresponds to each marker and how offsets map from the demonstrations; do not assume a fixed orientation or direction. Recolor each special marker to 4, extend its original marker color along the perpendicular ray toward its associated border, and draw the demonstrated full perpendicular line at the corresponding offset on the other segment. Preserve border cells and unrelated cells. Check the complete span and endpoints of every projected line: a line may extend across the grid to an edge where no border segment is present. Validate marker recoloring, segment-relative coordinate mapping, ray direction, and line endpoints against the examples before applying the rule.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"The demonstrations establish a reusable geometric rule, and the solved test confirms the importance of checking full projected-line endpoints rather than stopping at the extent of a border segment.","after":{"id":"arc_project_marker_rays_between_offset_border_segments","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: project marker rays between offset parallel border segments","content":"For ARC grids where demonstrations show two equal-length, parallel, offset border segments and special-color markers, consider a projection rule. Infer which segment corresponds to each marker and how offsets map from the demonstrations; do not assume a fixed orientation or direction. Recolor each special marker to 4, extend its original marker color along the perpendicular ray toward its associated border, and draw the demonstrated full perpendicular line at the corresponding offset on the other segment. Preserve border cells and unrelated cells. Check the complete span and endpoints of every projected line: a line may extend across the grid to an edge where no border segment is present. Validate marker recoloring, segment-relative coordinate mapping, ray direction, and line endpoints against the examples before applying the rule.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:56:53.908Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:56:53.908Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
