C grids with a dominant uniform background color B and many scattered cells of one other color F, consider this recoloring rule when demonstrations support it: map every B cell to 0 and every F cell to B, preserving dimensions and positions. Demonstrated mappings include 2/5 -> 0/2, 1/5 -> 0/1, and 6/5 -> 0/6. Do not map scattered cells to a fixed color such as 2; their output color is the original background B. Treat a uniform background with exactly one exceptional cell as a distinct case: a demonstration with background 5 and one cell of 9 mapped 5 -> 9 and 9 -> 0, so do not assume the multi-speck rule applies there.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:02:24.254Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:02:24.254Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
