lors inside and outside them.","metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Demonstration pair and correct test submission for task-d9f428cb"},"reason":"Persist the explicitly requested, demonstration-verified rule for a recurring task, including safeguards against confusing noise with patch boundaries.","after":{"id":"arc_task_d9f428cb_restore_rectangular_patches","kind":"memory","title":"ARC task-d9f428cb: restore solid rectangular patches from noisy grids","content":"For recurring ARC task-d9f428cb, demonstrations show grids encoding solid, axis-aligned rectangular color patches amid noise. Restore supported patch interiors to their patch color and set cells outside the patches to the evident background color; preserve dimensions. Background and patch colors can vary between inputs. Infer rectangle bounds from repeated aligned evidence, treating anomalous interior cells as corruption and isolated exterior colors as noise. Do not assume every colored cell defines a patch or extend bounds based only on nearby noise; verify candidate edges and all clues against the demonstrations. In the solved 12×30 test, the background was 0; patches were color 8 at rows 2–5, columns 2–6; rows 3–6, columns 9–12; rows 8–9, columns 7–13; and color 1 at rows 0–6, columns 14–16; rows 1–2, columns 22–27; rows 4–8, columns 25–29; rows 4–9, columns 18–23; rows 7–11, columns 2–5 (zero-based inclusive coordinates). A demo used background 1 and patches of color 6, with stray colors inside and outside them.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Demonstration pair and correct test submission for task-d9f428cb"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:41:00.457Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:41:00.457Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json"