{"id":"refine_20260929135323943","summary":"Create a global memory for task-7b641055 describing the demonstrated rule for filling every enclosed background cavity with color 4.","rationale":"Four demonstrations show enclosed background regions filled with color 4 while outlines and other cells remain unchanged. The solved test had two cavities, and earlier incorrect submissions missed cavity cells or a separate cavity, supporting explicit checks for all bounded regions and complete fills.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances of task-7b641055 should identify every fully enclosed background region, fill all its cells with 4, and preserve the outlines and grid dimensions; validate by checking each region for missed cells.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_task_7b641055_fill_all_enclosed_cavities","title":"ARC task-7b641055: fill every enclosed cavity with color 4","content":"For recurring ARC task-7b641055, demonstrations show that every background-colored cell in a fully enclosed cavity formed by foreground linework is replaced with color 4. Preserve the outline, all cells outside the cavities, and the original grid dimensions. There may be multiple cavities in one input, and their sizes vary; identify all bounded regions and fill every cell in each region, not just one cavity or a subset of its interior. In the solved 16×11 test, color 4 filled the 2×3 cavity in the left frame and the 4×1 cavity at column 7, rows 9–12, enclosed by the vertical sides at columns 6 and 8 and horizontal caps at rows 8 and 13. Earlier incorrect attempts missed an interior cell or omitted a separate cavity, so verify complete coverage of every enclosed region before submitting.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Stable recurring-task rule supported by four demonstrations and a correct test submission; records the key completeness checks exposed by incorrect attempts.","after":{"id":"arc_task_7b641055_fill_all_enclosed_cavities","kind":"memory","title":"ARC task-7b641055: fill every enclosed cavity with color 4","content":"For recurring ARC task-7b641055, demonstrations show that every background-colored cell in a fully enclosed cavity formed by foreground linework is replaced with color 4. Preserve the outline, all cells outside the cavities, and the original grid dimensions. There may be multiple cavities in one input, and their sizes vary; identify all bounded regions and fill every cell in each region, not just one cavity or a subset of its interior. In the solved 16×11 test, color 4 filled the 2×3 cavity in the left frame and the 4×1 cavity at column 7, rows 9–12, enclosed by the vertical sides at columns 6 and 8 and horizontal caps at rows 8 and 13. Earlier incorrect attempts missed an interior cell or omitted a separate cavity, so verify complete coverage of every enclosed region before submitting.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:53:30.786Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:53:30.786Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929135907181","summary":"Updated the task-45495946 memory with the verified single-object recoloring and selection cautions.","rationale":"The instance was solved after two incorrect submissions: recoloring both isolated color-3 cells and recoloring a vertical domino were both wrong; the correct output changed only the lower, farther singleton to the L-marker color. The demonstrations likewise show a selected object changed while unrelated cells remain intact.","expectedOutcome":"Future solvers should use the L marker's color and demonstrated shape/location relationship to select one intended object, avoid blanket recoloring or unsupported duplicate-shape guesses, and preserve all other cells; validate the candidate against the demonstrations.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_task_45495946_recolor_shape_match_with_L_marker_color","title":"ARC task-45495946: recolor the demonstrated matching object using the L-marker color","content":"For recurring ARC task-45495946, the L-shaped marker supplies the recolor color, but its presence does not justify recoloring every singleton or selecting an object based only on an assumed duplicate shape. Use the demonstrations to identify the intended object from its pattern and relationship to the marker, and change only that selected object; preserve dimensions and all unrelated cells. Verified test evidence: the marker was an upper-right L of color 5, and two isolated color-3 cells occurred at (0,19) and (18,16). The correct output changed only the lower, farther singleton at (18,16) to 5 and preserved the near singleton and all other cells. Recoloring both singletons and recoloring the distant vertical color-3 domino were incorrect. Do not generalize this test's farther/lower selection as a universal rule; determine the selected object from the task's demonstrations.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Records the verified successful transformation and guards against the specific unsupported selection strategies that failed in this instance.","before":{"id":"arc_task_45495946_recolor_shape_match_with_L_marker_color","kind":"memory","title":"ARC task-45495946: recolor the matching object using the L-marker color","content":"For recurring ARC task task-45495946, identify the conspicuous L-shaped marker/object and use its color as the recolor color. Find the separate object whose occupied-cell pattern matches the other reference/template shape, then recolor the matching object while preserving all unrelated cells and grid dimensions. In the solved test, the top-left color-4 pattern (2x5: full row, then all but second cell) matched the lower color-9 object at rows 6-7, cols 3-7; recoloring that object to color 5 was wrong, while recoloring it to color 7 (the large top-left L marker) was correct. Demos support the marker-color rule: a matching 9 object changed to color 0; a matching 7 object changed to color 5; and other selected objects changed to colors of L-like markers (e.g. 6, 3, 8). Caution: not every apparent L-shaped component is necessarily the marker, and demos include multiple objects; use the prominent marker + exact shape match rather than changing all similar-looking objects. Verify the candidate shape cell-for-cell and preserve all other objects.","path":"arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"task_id":"task-45495946","version":1},"source":"agent","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:39:38.530002+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:39:38.530019+00:00","version":1},"after":{"id":"arc_task_45495946_recolor_shape_match_with_L_marker_color","kind":"memory","title":"ARC task-45495946: recolor the demonstrated matching object using the L-marker color","content":"For recurring ARC task-45495946, the L-shaped marker supplies the recolor color, but its presence does not justify recoloring every singleton or selecting an object based only on an assumed duplicate shape. Use the demonstrations to identify the intended object from its pattern and relationship to the marker, and change only that selected object; preserve dimensions and all unrelated cells. Verified test evidence: the marker was an upper-right L of color 5, and two isolated color-3 cells occurred at (0,19) and (18,16). The correct output changed only the lower, farther singleton at (18,16) to 5 and preserved the near singleton and all other cells. Recoloring both singletons and recoloring the distant vertical color-3 domino were incorrect. Do not generalize this test's farther/lower selection as a universal rule; determine the selected object from the task's demonstrations.","path":"arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:39:38.530002+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:59:14.277Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
