nteriors filled with color 7; even side lengths (such as 4×4 or 6×6) have their interiors filled with color 2. Demonstrations support 3×3 and 5×5 frames filled with 7 and 4×4 and 6×6 frames filled with 2. Measure the outer frame, not the interior dimensions, and leave non-frame cells unchanged.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Two demonstrations and a correctly solved test instance"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:28:48.574Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:28:48.574Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929143023215","summary":"Update the global task-b50dfd4d memory with the verified stripe-placement rule and cautions from this solved instance.","rationale":"The trajectory confirms that a full color-2 divider cues adding a full-length color-8 stripe parallel to it, immediately beyond the separate object's farthest extent on the side away from the divider. The solved case and demos also expose wrong-color and off-by-one placement errors.","expectedOutcome":"Future task-b50dfd4d instances should preserve the input object and divider, place the color-8 stripe on the correct side at the correct zero-based index, and validate its orientation and position against the examples.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_task_b50dfd4d_add_full_color_8_line_beyond_object_across_divider_axis","title":"ARC task-b50dfd4d: add a color-8 stripe beyond the object, away from the divider","content":"For recurring ARC task-b50dfd4d, a full straight color-2 line is a divider and a separate colored object lies on one side. Add a full-length color-8 stripe parallel to the divider, immediately beyond the object's farthest extent on the side away from the divider. Preserve the divider, object, and all other cells. Verified examples: vertical divider at column 9 with object occupying columns 7–8 => add column 6 across all rows; horizontal divider at row 14 with object at row 13 => add row 12; vertical divider at column 22 with object occupying columns 17–21 => add column 16. In the solved test, the divider was at column 9 and the object extended to column 7, so the stripe belonged at column 6. Use zero-based indices and check the stripe coordinate carefully: an earlier submission used the wrong stripe color, and another used an incorrect column. The demonstrated stripe color is always 8.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Incorporates the verified solved case, multiple orientations and placements from demos, and specific errors observed during t