{"id":"refine_20260929143130424","summary":"Created a global memory for ARC task-1c897e72’s verified 3×3 block decoding rule.","rationale":"The task was solved correctly using 3×3 blocks: ignore noisy colors 0 and 5, and represent each block by its remaining signal color, or 0 when none is present. The demo and test support this rule.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances can be reduced to a grid one-third the input height and width by decoding each 3×3 block; validate dimensions and ensure 0 and 5 are never treated as signals.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_task_1c897e72_decode_3x3_blocks_ignoring_noise","title":"ARC task-1c897e72: decode 3×3 blocks while ignoring noise colors 0 and 5","content":"For recurring ARC task-1c897e72, divide the input into non-overlapping 3×3 blocks aligned from the top-left. Produce an output whose height and width are each one-third of the input dimensions. Colors 0 and 5 are noise/background, not signals. In each block, ignore 0 and 5 and output the most frequent remaining color; output 0 if no other color occurs. A verified 15×15 demo produced a 5×5 output with color 8 only at the block containing 8. A verified 27×27 test produced a 9×9 output using signal colors 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, and 8, and the submission was correct. Check that dimensions are divisible by 3 and do not count 0 or 5 as signals.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Preserves the demonstrated and test-verified block-decoding rule for future instances of this recurring task.","after":{"id":"arc_task_1c897e72_decode_3x3_blocks_ignoring_noise","kind":"memory","title":"ARC task-1c897e72: decode 3×3 blocks while ignoring noise colors 0 and 5","content":"For recurring ARC task-1c897e72, divide the input into non-overlapping 3×3 blocks aligned from the top-left. Produce an output whose height and width are each one-third of the input dimensions. Colors 0 and 5 are noise/background, not signals. In each block, ignore 0 and 5 and output the most frequent remaining color; output 0 if no other color occurs. A verified 15×15 demo produced a 5×5 output with color 8 only at the block containing 8. A verified 27×27 test produced a 9×9 output using signal colors 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, and 8, and the submission was correct. Check that dimensions are divisible by 3 and do not count 0 or 5 as signals.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:31:37.480Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:31:37.480Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
