tile in the same orientation, preserving all dividers and grid dimensions. Demonstrations: with a vertical divider, the populated tile is copied unchanged across it; with vertical and horizontal dividers, the upper-left pattern is repeated unchanged in the other three tiles. A solved 11×13 instance had a 3×6 source tile in the upper-left and repeated it into all six tiles. Do not reflect or rotate the pattern. Carefully check tile boundaries, separator positions, and row widths.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:32:53.789Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:32:53.789Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929143443690","summary":"Updated the global task-45495946 memory with the verified directional selection rule and failed-guess cautions.","rationale":"Four demonstrations and the solved test show that the L marker’s color is applied to the object indicated outward beyond its arms, not necessarily the nearest object or one inside the L’s corner; two incorrect submissions confirm those selection mistakes.","expectedOutcome":"Future task-45495946 instances should preserve the L marker and unrelated cells, use its color to recolor only the indicated separate object, and avoid selecting by proximity alone; validate the direction against the L orientation and demonstrations.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_task_45495946_recolor_shape_match_with_L_marker_color","title":"ARC task-45495946: recolor the object indicated outward by the L marker","content":"For recurring ARC task-45495946, use the L-shaped marker's color to recolor the separate object it indicates, preserving the marker and all other cells. Determine the indicated direction from the L orientation: the target lies outward beyond one or both arms, in the directional continuation away from the corner-facing region. Do not assume the target is nearest or select an object merely because it lies inside the L's corner. Demonstrations establish this across orientations: (1) an upper-left color-3 L indicated a distant lower-right vertical color-8 object; (2) an upper-left color-1 L indicated the upper vertical color-4 component at upper-right, not the lower color-4 component; (3) a lower-left color-5 L indicated the upper color-2 component, not the nearby lower color-2 component; (4) a lower-right color-1 L indicated an upper-left vertical color-0 object. In the solved test, the color-5 L had arms up and right and indicated the down-right color-9 pair, which was recolored to 5. Recoloring the upper-right color-4 pair or lower-left color-2 block in that test was incorrect. Preserve grid dimensions and every non-target cell.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Adds verified selection evidence and cautions to the existing task-specific memory after two incorrect target selections and a correct solution.","before":{"id":"arc_task_45495946_recolor_shape_match_with_L_marker_color","kind":"memory","title":"ARC task-45495946: use L marker color to recolor the selected separate object","content":"For recurring ARC task-45495946, identify the L-shaped marker and use its color as the replacement color for the selected separate object. The marker guides selection, but do not recolor every object of another color or assume that the target must duplicate the L's shape. Across demos, the target varied widely in color and shape: (1) color-1 L, recolor one large color-4 component near the lower-left; (2) color-2 L, recolor the 2x2 color-4 block (not the nearby singleton); (3) color-5 L, recolor the selected color-9 cluster; (4) color-7 L, recolor the 2x3 color-8 block. In the solved 21x11 case, color 4 formed an L at rows 13-20, cols 7-10; the intended object was the isolated color-1 cell at (9,3), recolored to 4. A tempting lower singleton at (19,9) was wrong. The marker-object spatial relationship appears important (often the target lies in the direction indicated by the L's open side), but demonstrations show this is not a simple universal nearest-object or exact-shape rule. Select one target using the full layout and preserve all other cells and dimensions. Prior validated case also showed that among isolated candidate cells, only the intended one should change; recoloring both isolated candidates or a separate vertical domino was wrong.","path":"arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"agent","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:39:38.530002+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:27:17.816991+00:00","version":3},"after":{"id":"arc_task_45495946_recolor_shape_match_with_L_marker_color","kind":"memory","title":"ARC task-45495946: recolor the object indicated outward by the L marker","content":"For recurring ARC task-45495946, use the L-shaped marker's color to recolor the separate object it indicates, preserving the marker and all other cells. Determine the indicated direction from the L orientation: the target lies outward beyond one or both arms, in the directional continuation away from the corner-facing region. Do not assume the target is nearest or select an object merely because it lies inside the L's corner. Demonstrations establish this across orientations: (1) an upper-left color-3 L indicated a distant lower-right vertical color-8 object; (2) an upper-left color-1 L indicated the upper vertical color-4 component at upper-right, not the lower color-4 component; (3) a lower-left color-5 L indicated the upper color-2 component, not the nearby lower color-2 component; (4) a lower-right color-1 L indicated an upper-left vertical color-0 object. In the solved test, the color-5 L had arms up and right and indicated the down-right color-9 pair, which was recolored to 5. Recoloring the upper-right color-4 pair or lower-left color-2 block in that test was incorrect. Preserve grid dimensions and every non-target cell.","path":"arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:39:38.530002+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:34:51.340Z","version":4},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929143650307","summary":"Updated the existing global memory for ARC task-14326ef7 with the demo-verified aligned background-intersection rule.","rationale":"The current trajectory confirms outputs mark color 3 only where both aligned panels contain their shared background color; the earlier task memory describes a different shared-color comparison rule, so updating it avoids retaining conflicting guidance.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances should identify the separator and panel orientation, align equal-sized panels, and mark only the intersection of their shared-background cells; validate output dimensions and the rule against all demonstrations.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_task_14326ef7_compare_aligned_panels_shared_color","title":"ARC task-14326ef7: mark aligned shared-background intersection","content":"For recurring ARC task-14326ef7, demonstrations show an input split into equal-sized panels by a uniform separator, horizontal or vertical. The first panel is a binary guide with a common background color B and sparse accent cells; the second panel uses B as its background plus another color. Output has the dimensions of one panel: at each aligned coordinate, write color 3 if BOTH panels contain B, and otherwise write B. Preserve no separator in the output. Demo 1: vertical separator 9; guide background 8 with sparse 4; target colors 2/8; output is 3 where both panels are 8, else 8. Demo 2: horizontal separator 9; guide background 0 with sparse 4; target colors 0/5; output is 3 where both panels are 0, else 0. The 15×11 test also followed this rule with guide background 5/accent 7 and target colors 5/6. Do not simply swap target colors or mark panel equality independent of the shared-background condition.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Replace conflicting earlier task guidance with the rule supported by both requested demonstrations and the correctly solved test.","before":{"id":"arc_task_14326ef7_compare_aligned_panels_shared_color","kind":"memory","title":"ARC task-14326ef7: compare aligned panels using their shared palette color","content":"For recurring ARC task-14326ef7, the input has two aligned panels separated by a uniform divider row or column. Identify the panel orientation and corresponding cells; the output has the dimensions of one panel. The two panel palettes have a unique color in common. Initialize every output cell to that shared color, then write color 3 wherever the corresponding input cells are equal. Compare actual cell colors, not just foreground/background occupancy. Do not assume the output background is the dominant color of the right or bottom panel. Six demos support the rule; in the solved test, the shared color was 0 and equal 0/0 cells became 3.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:14:36.356Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:14:36.356Z","version":1},"after":{"id":"arc_task_14326ef7_compare_aligned_panels_shared_color","kind":"memory","title":"ARC task-14326ef7: mark aligned shared-background intersection","content":"For recurring ARC task-14326ef7, demonstrations show an input split into equal-sized panels by a uniform separator, horizontal or vertical. The first panel is a binary guide with a common background color B and sparse accent cells; the second panel uses B as its background plus another color. Output has the dimensions of one panel: at each aligned coordinate, write color 3 if BOTH panels contain B, and otherwise write B. Preserve no separator in the output. Demo 1: vertical separator 9; guide background 8 with sparse 4; target colors 2/8; output is 3 where both panels are 8, else 8. Demo 2: horizontal separator 9; guide background 0 with sparse 4; target colors 0/5; output is 3 where both panels are 0, else 0. The 15×11 test also followed this rule with guide background 5/accent 7 and target colors 5/6. Do not simply swap target colors or mark panel equality independent of the shared-background condition.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:14:36.356Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:36:58.696Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682248/attempts/6d3823d65d4947dd91c6d88a902b3f7d/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
